# shadcn/ui (dashboard)

Full detail lives in **`.claude/skills/shadcn/rules/`** (`composition.md`, `base-vs-radix.md`, `styling.md`, `forms.md`, `icons.md`). This file is the **condensed** checklist.

## Radix vs `base` UI

- Run `npx shadcn@latest info` and check the **`base`** field for this project.
- **Radix:** triggers use **`asChild`** (no extra wrapper divs). **`Select`:** items inline in JSX.
- **Base:** triggers use **`render={<Button />}`**; non-button targets need **`nativeButton={false}`**. **`Select`** needs an **`items`** prop; still wrap items in **`SelectGroup`** inside content.

## Composition (both)

- Menu/list items: wrap in **Group** (`SelectGroup`, `DropdownMenuGroup`, etc.) — never loose items only in the scroll container.
- **Dialog / Sheet / Drawer:** always include a **Title** (use `className="sr-only"` if hidden). Prefer **AlertDialog** for destructive confirms.
- **Card:** `CardHeader` + `CardTitle` / `CardDescription`, `CardContent`, optional `CardFooter`.
- **Tabs:** `TabsTrigger` only inside **`TabsList`**.
- **Avatar:** always **`AvatarFallback`**.
- **Button:** no built-in `isLoading` — use **`Spinner`** + **`disabled`** + `data-icon` (see icons rule).
- Prefer **Separator**, **Skeleton**, **Badge** over hand-rolled `hr` / pulse divs / styled spans.

## Styling

- Use **semantic** classes (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `text-destructive`) and component **variants**, not raw `bg-blue-500` for product UI.
- Use **`cn()`** for conditional classes. Avoid **`space-x-*` / `space-y-*`** in shadcn layouts where the skill says to use gap/stack patterns.
- Do not assign manual **z-index** on overlays; use library stacking.

## Forms

- Prefer **`FieldGroup` + `Field` + `FieldLabel`** over ad-hoc `div` + `space-y-*`.
- Inside **`InputGroup`**, use **`InputGroupInput`** / **`InputGroupTextarea`**, not raw `Input`.

## Icons (this project: lucide-react)

- In **Button** (and similar): **`data-icon="inline-start"`** or **`inline-end`**; **no** `size-4` / `mr-2` on the icon unless the user explicitly wants custom sizing.

## Toasts

- Use **`sonner`** (`toast.success`, etc.) when the project already imports it — stay consistent with existing dashboard code.
